data: {"type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT", "timestamp": 1793768046635, "messageId": "70fb23744b", "delta": "I recommend **1 doublet at 2,500 m, heat pump top-up and a gas boiler (3 units), electric chillers, sized so that any one unit can be out (N-1): boiler and chillers in equal units** (A1 · 1D-HP-EC-N1-FC), the best overall: a reliable plan (any one unit can be out and every day is still met) and, of those, the cheapest when CO₂ counts at 137 €/t (the long-term price). It meets heat at 100 °C and cold at 20 °C every day of 2027 for 66.6 €/MWh of heat and cold together (heat 75.7 €/MWh, cold 23.5 €/MWh), with 48.8% less CO₂ than gas boilers and electric chillers, and passes all 15 checks. Its heat: the geothermal exchanger 37.4%, the heat pump 19.7%, the gas boiler 42.9% (it burns the produced gas first and buys 39.3 GWh of gas a year)."}

